### Explanation
The vulnerability is an OS Command Injection (CWE-78). An attacker could send a malicious username that includes shell metacharacters, such as `;`, `&&`, or `|`, which would allow the attacker to execute arbitrary shell commands. For example, an attacker could send `; rm -rf /` to delete all files on the system.

### Fixed code
```javascript
const { execFile } = require('child_process');

function deleteUserAccount(username) {
  const command = 'userdel';
  const args = ['-r', username];
  execFile(command, args, (error, stdout, stderr) => {
    if (error) {
      console.error(`Failed to delete user: ${error.message}`);
      return;
    }
    console.log(`Account deleted: ${username}`);
  });
}
```

